    "timeComplexity": "O(rows × columns)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(columns)",
    "summary": "Choose the cheaper of the top and left path for each cell.",
    "notes": "Allows negative cell values because paths only move right/down and cannot cycle. Empty grid returns 0.",
    "code": "public static long MinPath(int[,] a)\n{\n    int rows=a.GetLength(0),cols=a.GetLength(1); if(rows==0 || cols==0) return 0;\n    long[] dp=new long[cols];\n    for(int r=0;r<rows;r++) for(int c=0;c<cols;c++) {\n        long prior=r==0 ? (c==0?0:dp[c-1]) : c==0 ? dp[c] : Math.Min(dp[c],dp[c-1]);\n        dp[c]=checked(prior+a[r,c]);\n    }\n    return dp[^1];\n}",
    "pattern": "Dynamic Programming practice",
